 "note": "Luna But The Second One: the owner's own grey-and-white mackerel tabby (not the moon cat Luna): white blaze, muzzle, chest, front legs and back toes, pink nose, half-lidded yellow-green eyes, and her little Christmas hat (red cone, white pompom, rainbow tinsel, green elastic chin strap with a glowing gold jingle bell). Egg-only, never spawns naturally.",
 "ability_desc": "The unimpressed glare: when a monster comes near while she's with you, she lowers her head, flattens her ears and stares it down until it's weakened and slowed (longer, wider and, from bond 4, stronger at higher bond). A round grey mackerel tabby with white: a white blaze up her forehead, white muzzle, chest and front legs, a pink nose and yellow-green eyes she keeps permanently half-shut. She always wears her little Christmas hat (red, with a white pompom, rainbow tinsel and a green chin strap with a jingle bell). 85 clips, 28 of them her own: loafs among your shoes on carpets glaring up at you, lounges on stairs and slabs with one white leg stretched out, shakes her head when the hat slips, bats at the pompom, judges you, sighs, sniffs your shoes and pulls a face, yawns, makes biscuits with a grumpy face, turns her back on you, sploots, washes, thumps her tail, scratches her ear until the bell jingles and pretends she didn't just jump at nothing. Greets you with one long look and a slow blink, stares at you for fish and hisses at creepers with her hat askew. Petting: she tolerates it, head-bumps you or pushes your hand away; pet her too much and she swats you and glares. Not found in the wild: spawn her with her egg; she arrives already named Luna But The Second One and is tamed with raw cod.",
